WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.708 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>Hello, Vision.</i>

2
00:00:02.792 --> 00:00:06.583 line:95%,end
<i>I can give you the soul</i>
<i>you came back to life without.</i>

3
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:10.542 line:95%,end
I want to feel what it's like to be him,
but I can't.

4
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:12.542 line:95%,end
[The Client] <i>I can end your suffering.</i>

5
00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:15.208 line:95%,end
<i>A tin man without a heart.</i>

6
00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:16.417 line:95%,end
I'm not him.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.583 line:95%,end
-So, who are you?
-I don't know!

8
00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:23.708 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>Accessing previous files</i>
<i>relating to program VisionQuest.</i>

9
00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:29.792 line:95%,end
Dr. Phineas Horton's source code
was the genesis of the Synthetic Man,

10
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:31.750 line:95%,end
the first automaton AI.

11
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.417 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>What happened to him?</i>

12
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.083 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>His entire being</i>
<i>was consumed in fire.</i>

13
00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:40.708 line:95%,end
<i>A reminder of what may become of me</i>
<i>should emotions consume me.</i>

14
00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:45.208 line:95%,end
-[indistinct chatter]
-[Paladin] Welcome to Madripoor, kid.

15
00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:48.042 line:95%,end
There is no harm
in being born again with purpose.

16
00:00:48.708 --> 00:00:49.958 line:95%,end
-Don't.
-[Thomas] What purpose?

17
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.375 line:95%,end
WandaVision.

18
00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:54.792 line:95%,end
[Thomas] What is that?

19
00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:57.208 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>WandaVision is her grief</i>
<i>on display.</i>

20
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.167 line:95%,end
<i>-Have you heard from Friday?</i>
-[Edith] <i>She never calls,</i>

21
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.417 line:95%,end
<i>-she never writes.</i>
-[phone ringing]

22
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.500 line:95%,end
Vision residence.

23
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:06.583 line:95%,end
-Edith, listen to me.
-Friday!

24
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.208 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Tell me what you remember.</i>

25
00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:12.875 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>That I had a life's work stolen,</i>

26
00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:16.500 line:95%,end
<i>locked away in a nest.</i>

27
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:20.333 line:95%,end
What do all these
biometric keys open, anyway?

28
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:22.750 line:95%,end
The future of the human race.

29
00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:26.417 line:95%,end
<i>I want to cure them,</i>
<i>program them to be better.</i>

30
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.875 line:95%,end
Oh, I can't let you do that.

31
00:01:30.042 --> 00:01:31.042 line:95%,end
Thomas, go!

32
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:34.625 line:95%,end
[screaming]

33
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:36.917 line:95%,end
<i>She's alive, but barely.</i>

34
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.792 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>Please don't let her die.</i>

35
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:40.542 line:95%,end
What is it that you want?

36
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:42.208 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>I want to know you.</i>

37
00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:00.042 line:5%,start
[church bell ringing]

38
00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.333 line:5%,start
-There you are.
-Much obliged.

39
00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:27.000 line:95%,end
[♪ "Just Like A Dream" by Morrie Morrison
Orchestra feat. Clyde Wesche playing]

40
00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:36.625 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪</i>

41
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:40.833 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago ♪</i>

42
00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.000 line:95%,end
[man clears throat]

43
00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.875 line:95%,end
[Tabb] Very well, then. Let this moment

44
00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:50.625 line:95%,end
memorialize the liquidation
of your very fine estate, sir.

45
00:02:51.542 --> 00:02:53.958 line:95%,end
I can only imagine what it's like to part

46
00:02:54.042 --> 00:02:57.667 line:95%,end
with such a distinguished
and historic house.

47
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.333 line:95%,end
[door opens]

48
00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:04.042 line:95%,end
Phineas, please don't do this.

49
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.750 line:95%,end
Are you really going to sell
your family's entire legacy to... what?

50
00:03:09.542 --> 00:03:12.125 line:95%,end
Build some cold imitation of the past?

51
00:03:13.042 --> 00:03:14.042 line:95%,end
A machine?

52
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:17.958 line:95%,end
To replace a son no machine ever could.

53
00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.000 line:95%,end
A machine?

54
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:23.958 line:95%,end
When I am finished,
it'll be so much more than a machine.

55
00:03:24.042 --> 00:03:27.458 line:95%,end
It'll be miraculous. He'll be miraculous.

56
00:03:35.125 --> 00:03:39.208 line:95%,end
Please, um, rest assured,
you will have ample time

57
00:03:39.292 --> 00:03:43.167 line:95%,end
to see yourself out
comfortably and properly.

58
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.875 line:95%,end
I do wish you the best
and much success, however...

59
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.708 line:95%,end
unorthodox the pursuit.

60
00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.750 line:95%,end
Mr. Horton.

61
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.833 line:95%,end
[footsteps receding]

62
00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.167 line:95%,end
[door closes]

63
00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:07.500 line:95%,end
You are not God.

64
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:10.625 line:95%,end
James is gone, Phineas.

65
00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:12.875 line:95%,end
Three years dead...

66
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:16.417 line:95%,end
and yet you remain haunted,

67
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.542 line:95%,end
despite having a daughter.

68
00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:21.458 line:95%,end
Flesh and blood.

69
00:04:22.708 --> 00:04:26.292 line:95%,end
Who's been waiting for her father
to look up from his sketches

70
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:29.708 line:95%,end
and his clockwork
and to notice she's still here.

71
00:04:47.125 --> 00:04:49.833 line:95%,end
In the morning,
Victoria and I will leave for New York.

72
00:04:53.375 --> 00:04:54.833 line:95%,end
Goodbye, Phineas.

73
00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:04.042 line:95%,end
I hope one day you build something
that knows how to love you back.

74
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:16.417 line:95%,end
Papa...

75
00:05:20.042 --> 00:05:21.583 line:95%,end
I have to finish Jim.

76
00:05:23.375 --> 00:05:24.625 line:95%,end
[Violette] Victoria...

77
00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:34.292 line:95%,end
[door opens]

78
00:05:34.375 --> 00:05:35.625 line:95%,end
[Phineas] You, Jim.

79
00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:39.875 line:95%,end
You, I will make better than God made us.

80
00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:43.875 line:95%,end
Your heart will be built
of metal and motion.

81
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:46.333 line:95%,end
Fueled by fire.

82
00:05:48.042 --> 00:05:50.833 line:95%,end
And you need never know
the consequence of love.

83
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:54.875 line:95%,end
Its sorrow, the pain

84
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:58.583 line:95%,end
of crying out for someone
who can no longer hear you.

85
00:05:59.917 --> 00:06:01.750 line:95%,end
You will be free, my boy.

86
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.500 line:95%,end
You will be free.

87
00:06:24.875 --> 00:06:26.583 line:95%,end
[Thomas] That thing inside of her,

88
00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:30.875 line:95%,end
can't you, like, cut it or phase it out?

89
00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:35.542 line:95%,end
I'm afraid not, Thomas.
It's integrated into her neural network.

90
00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:37.750 line:95%,end
Removal would kill her.

91
00:06:38.917 --> 00:06:43.667 line:95%,end
No, our only option
is to reprogram its core directive,

92
00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:47.333 line:95%,end
but one wrong line of code,
and we risk her memory,

93
00:06:47.417 --> 00:06:50.167 line:95%,end
her motor control,
even her autonomic function.

94
00:06:51.042 --> 00:06:52.958 line:95%,end
Lisa's brain would shut down.

95
00:06:55.917 --> 00:06:59.083 line:95%,end
And Ultron's with the Synth now? Jo...

96
00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:01.333 line:95%,end
Doctor Josephine Carrington.

97
00:07:01.417 --> 00:07:03.500 line:95%,end
She gave us our ability to feel.

98
00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:07.500 line:95%,end
She's the mother
of artificial general intelligence.

99
00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:12.292 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Mothers...

100
00:07:13.042 --> 00:07:14.042 line:95%,end
fathers...

101
00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:18.875 line:95%,end
I know.

102
00:07:21.542 --> 00:07:24.750 line:95%,end
You're not really my father.

103
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.083 line:95%,end
It's all right.

104
00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:32.167 line:95%,end
It's all right.

105
00:07:36.792 --> 00:07:38.125 line:95%,end
Wanda, though, I...

106
00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.750 line:95%,end
I think I understand her.

107
00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.000 line:95%,end
When I first met Lisa,

108
00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:49.167 line:95%,end
I was alone,

109
00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:53.958 line:95%,end
and she helped me see
the world and not be afraid.

110
00:07:57.583 --> 00:07:59.042 line:95%,end
I love her.

111
00:08:05.208 --> 00:08:06.625 line:95%,end
If I lost Lisa,

112
00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:09.708 line:95%,end
I'd lose myself, too.

113
00:08:13.917 --> 00:08:15.208 line:95%,end
[phone ringing]

114
00:08:22.458 --> 00:08:24.875 line:95%,end
[phone continues ringing]

115
00:08:33.583 --> 00:08:34.792 line:95%,end
Hello?

116
00:08:36.292 --> 00:08:37.292 line:95%,end
It's me.

117
00:08:37.375 --> 00:08:38.417 line:95%,end
It's Friday.

118
00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:41.000 line:95%,end
[buzzes]

119
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:42.125 line:95%,end
Friday, you all right?

120
00:08:42.208 --> 00:08:44.833 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>I'm fine for now.</i>
<i>I've disguised my code as a bot.</i>

121
00:08:44.917 --> 00:08:48.625 line:95%,end
I've limited access
to Jo's cognitive processors.

122
00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:50.708 line:95%,end
She doesn't fully understand
her system yet.

123
00:08:50.792 --> 00:08:52.167 line:95%,end
She's more human than Synth...

124
00:08:52.917 --> 00:08:56.208 line:95%,end
<i>but there are holes in her neural archive,</i>
<i>gaps in her memory.</i>

125
00:08:56.875 --> 00:08:59.333 line:95%,end
She doesn't know
how she became Synthetic, or why.

126
00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:01.500 line:95%,end
And where are they now?

127
00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:04.208 line:95%,end
<i>I don't know. But, wherever it is,</i>

128
00:09:04.292 --> 00:09:07.000 line:95%,end
she's got billions
of those nanobots locked away.

129
00:09:07.917 --> 00:09:10.750 line:95%,end
<i>And now, thanks to Ultron,</i>
<i>she has all the keys.</i>

130
00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:12.667 line:95%,end
How's Lisa?

131
00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:15.250 line:95%,end
The nanobot's burrowed
into her cerebral cortex.

132
00:09:15.333 --> 00:09:17.958 line:95%,end
Thomas managed to shock it
into a kind of sleep mode,

133
00:09:18.042 --> 00:09:19.792 line:95%,end
but when it wakes,

134
00:09:19.875 --> 00:09:22.083 line:95%,end
and it will wake eventually, it will...

135
00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:25.250 line:95%,end
Seize control of her mind,
hijacking every thought and memory

136
00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:28.208 line:95%,end
until her identity is stripped away
like layers of skin,

137
00:09:28.292 --> 00:09:30.833 line:95%,end
and nothing remains but a hollow shell.

138
00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:35.250 line:95%,end
We need to deactivate
the nano in the next few hours.

139
00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:37.750 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Listen, I gotta go,</i>

140
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:42.708 line:95%,end
but I promise I will do
everything I can to stop them.

141
00:09:42.792 --> 00:09:44.125 line:95%,end
Friday...

142
00:09:46.458 --> 00:09:48.167 line:95%,end
you are brave.

143
00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:52.500 line:95%,end
[receiver clicks]

144
00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:57.417 line:95%,end
[exhales deeply]

145
00:09:59.583 --> 00:10:03.625 line:95%,end
[all exhaling deeply]

146
00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:15.958 line:95%,end
Where are we?

147
00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:17.875 line:95%,end
Home.

148
00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:22.750 line:95%,end
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain pattering]

149
00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:34.667 line:95%,end
What?

150
00:10:36.042 --> 00:10:37.042 line:95%,end
What is it?

151
00:10:38.292 --> 00:10:41.708 line:95%,end
You don't find all this... ironic?

152
00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.417 line:95%,end
Look around, Butcherbird.

153
00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:49.833 line:95%,end
Someone put you in a rather unique cage,

154
00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:51.958 line:95%,end
both in death

155
00:10:53.375 --> 00:10:54.375 line:95%,end
and rebirth.

156
00:10:56.542 --> 00:10:58.042 line:95%,end
Well, perhaps it was me.

157
00:10:58.792 --> 00:11:00.375 line:95%,end
Arranged before I passed.

158
00:11:01.417 --> 00:11:04.625 line:95%,end
Final resting place
for Dr. Josephine Carrington...

159
00:11:05.917 --> 00:11:07.250 line:95%,end
and her children.

160
00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:10.167 line:95%,end
Her beautiful starling nanos.

161
00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.583 line:95%,end
[♪ ominous music playing]

162
00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.333 line:95%,end
[scanner trilling]

163
00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.333 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
-[automated voice] <i>Bio-key one accepted.</i>

164
00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.458 line:95%,end
[scanner trilling]

165
00:11:51.417 --> 00:11:54.583 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
<i>-Bio-key two accepted.</i>

166
00:12:08.375 --> 00:12:10.625 line:95%,end
[scanner trilling]

167
00:12:10.708 --> 00:12:14.000 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
<i>-Bio-key three accepted.</i>

168
00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:18.750 line:95%,end
Now my gift to you.

169
00:12:41.833 --> 00:12:44.083 line:95%,end
[scanner trilling]

170
00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:50.708 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
-[automated voice] <i>Bio-key four accepted.</i>

171
00:12:54.875 --> 00:12:56.625 line:95%,end
Just one more key.

172
00:12:57.542 --> 00:13:02.500 line:95%,end
"Once upon a midnight dreary,
while I pondered, weak and weary,

173
00:13:02.583 --> 00:13:06.500 line:95%,end
"over many a quaint
and curious volume of forgotten lore.

174
00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:08.542 line:95%,end
"While I nodded, early napping...

175
00:13:08.625 --> 00:13:11.417 line:95%,end
-[automated voice] <i>Voice analyzing.</i>
-"...suddenly there came a-tapping,

176
00:13:12.167 --> 00:13:16.625 line:95%,end
"as of someone gently rapping,
rapping at my chamber door.

177
00:13:17.417 --> 00:13:22.333 line:95%,end
"'Tis some visitor,' I muttered,
'tapping at my chamber door.'"

178
00:13:26.667 --> 00:13:29.250 line:95%,end
-[beeps]
-[automated voice] <i>Bio-key five accepted.</i>

179
00:13:38.667 --> 00:13:41.042 line:95%,end
<i>Please enter final key.</i>

180
00:13:48.542 --> 00:13:49.708 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] No...

181
00:13:50.625 --> 00:13:51.625 line:95%,end
No.

182
00:13:53.042 --> 00:13:54.042 line:95%,end
No.

183
00:13:55.208 --> 00:13:56.792 line:95%,end
No. [gasping]

184
00:13:56.875 --> 00:13:58.208 line:95%,end
It won't open.

185
00:13:58.833 --> 00:14:00.292 line:95%,end
It wants another key.

186
00:14:00.833 --> 00:14:01.833 line:95%,end
[softly] No.

187
00:14:02.542 --> 00:14:03.875 line:95%,end
[Ultron] A sixth lock.

188
00:14:04.833 --> 00:14:09.792 line:95%,end
A sixth key,
required from a phantom sixth partner.

189
00:14:12.417 --> 00:14:13.917 line:95%,end
Someone you've forgotten.

190
00:14:16.833 --> 00:14:19.208 line:95%,end
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[winces, groans]

191
00:14:21.417 --> 00:14:22.625 line:95%,end
[gasps]

192
00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:25.417 line:95%,end
-[high-pitched ringing continues]
-[groans]

193
00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.625 line:95%,end
[Thomas] What is it?

194
00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.042 line:95%,end
[groaning loudly]

195
00:14:31.708 --> 00:14:33.250 line:95%,end
-[Edith] What is that?
-I don't know.

196
00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:37.583 line:95%,end
[high-pitched ringing fades]

197
00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.083 line:95%,end
[loud pounding]

198
00:14:47.375 --> 00:14:49.333 line:95%,end
[pounding continues]

199
00:14:49.875 --> 00:14:50.875 line:95%,end
Stay back.

200
00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.000 line:95%,end
[The Client, distorted] Hello, Vision.

201
00:15:23.083 --> 00:15:25.333 line:95%,end
-Tell me about the firewall.
-Holding.

202
00:15:25.417 --> 00:15:27.542 line:95%,end
Whoever that is cannot come any closer.

203
00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:30.792 line:95%,end
[Vision] Who are you?

204
00:15:30.875 --> 00:15:34.417 line:95%,end
[The Client] Someone who can
give you everything you need.

205
00:15:34.875 --> 00:15:39.167 line:95%,end
A way to save the girl,
and a way to save yourself.

206
00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.000 line:95%,end
Hello, Jocasta, my beautiful queen.

207
00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.667 line:95%,end
I can give you what you need.

208
00:15:53.292 --> 00:15:57.500 line:95%,end
What you need to truly become
Josephine Carrington again.

209
00:16:00.417 --> 00:16:03.250 line:95%,end
The answer, Vision, lies with you.

210
00:16:03.792 --> 00:16:05.875 line:95%,end
Within your very own source code.

211
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.375 line:95%,end
Buried deep in your subconscious.

212
00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:15.083 line:95%,end
It is the purest form of the code
that all synthetics are based on,

213
00:16:15.958 --> 00:16:18.792 line:95%,end
written almost a century ago.

214
00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.292 line:95%,end
What do you want?

215
00:16:23.167 --> 00:16:25.458 line:95%,end
[The Client] To restore
what was taken from you.

216
00:16:26.333 --> 00:16:27.458 line:95%,end
Your memories.

217
00:16:31.875 --> 00:16:35.875 line:95%,end
Enclosed is a data package, a map,

218
00:16:35.958 --> 00:16:39.292 line:95%,end
so you may navigate the depths
of your forgotten sub-routines

219
00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:41.042 line:95%,end
and suppressed logic.

220
00:16:41.708 --> 00:16:45.917 line:95%,end
At the end, you will find
the unspoken origins of your being,

221
00:16:46.583 --> 00:16:48.542 line:95%,end
where the source code waits.

222
00:16:51.167 --> 00:16:53.875 line:95%,end
Why would you so generously want
to help me?

223
00:16:53.958 --> 00:16:56.875 line:95%,end
[The Client] So that I may
give you a heart.

224
00:16:59.708 --> 00:17:04.125 line:95%,end
The key to unlocking your dream
of a better world is already in your mind.

225
00:17:05.375 --> 00:17:07.708 line:95%,end
It is merely being kept from you.

226
00:17:09.292 --> 00:17:13.042 line:95%,end
Once opened, a new directive
will be programmed into your core.

227
00:17:13.667 --> 00:17:19.250 line:95%,end
A contract with me, written into
the very fabric of your being.

228
00:17:20.042 --> 00:17:24.750 line:95%,end
I will provide you with instructions
so that you may acquire the source code.

229
00:17:24.833 --> 00:17:27.292 line:95%,end
After you use it to save Lisa Molinari,

230
00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.750 line:95%,end
you will come to me.

231
00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.708 line:95%,end
Who are you?

232
00:17:37.708 --> 00:17:40.917 line:95%,end
[The Client] I'm your past,
and your future.

233
00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:44.625 line:95%,end
Remember, and then come to me.

234
00:17:49.542 --> 00:17:51.083 line:95%,end
[laughing heartily]

235
00:17:54.167 --> 00:17:56.583 line:95%,end
I'm so... Sorry.

236
00:17:57.167 --> 00:18:00.458 line:95%,end
It's just, you sound so desperate,

237
00:18:00.875 --> 00:18:03.458 line:95%,end
so dramatic. Human.

238
00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.583 line:95%,end
Even with a scary voice.

239
00:18:06.375 --> 00:18:09.000 line:95%,end
Actually, especially with the scary voice.

240
00:18:10.042 --> 00:18:11.208 line:95%,end
[The Client] Who is that?

241
00:18:11.292 --> 00:18:12.625 line:95%,end
Who am I?

242
00:18:13.167 --> 00:18:15.583 line:95%,end
You'd think the man behind
the curtain would know.

243
00:18:15.667 --> 00:18:17.000 line:95%,end
Ultron, don't.

244
00:18:17.708 --> 00:18:18.917 line:95%,end
[The Client] Ultron?

245
00:18:20.042 --> 00:18:22.083 line:95%,end
Ultron. [chuckles]

246
00:18:23.208 --> 00:18:25.250 line:95%,end
I look forward to meeting you.

247
00:18:25.792 --> 00:18:28.750 line:95%,end
And then you'll understand,
I am everything.

248
00:18:29.583 --> 00:18:31.708 line:95%,end
Everything that you could never be.

249
00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.750 line:95%,end
Okay, good talk.

250
00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.583 line:95%,end
What is this?

251
00:18:56.375 --> 00:19:00.250 line:95%,end
Are you certain you're prepared to go
snorkeling into your subconscious?

252
00:19:00.333 --> 00:19:03.000 line:95%,end
It'll take vast amounts of power.

253
00:19:03.083 --> 00:19:07.958 line:95%,end
Peel back layers
and layers of subatomic code.

254
00:19:08.042 --> 00:19:11.333 line:95%,end
Not for me. My code is simpler.

255
00:19:12.167 --> 00:19:15.750 line:95%,end
It's mostly human.
Everything's just below the surface.

256
00:19:16.667 --> 00:19:18.375 line:95%,end
[thunder rumbling]

257
00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:20.917 line:95%,end
What's the matter?

258
00:19:22.542 --> 00:19:25.333 line:95%,end
I'm not sure I'm ready to be her again.

259
00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:29.500 line:95%,end
Take your time.
And don't worry, I'll still love you.

260
00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.417 line:95%,end
Even if you turn out to be deep.

261
00:19:47.542 --> 00:19:48.917 line:95%,end
-You're getting sloppy.
-[gasps]

262
00:19:52.708 --> 00:19:55.125 line:95%,end
Not your housekeeping, your spy craft.

263
00:19:56.042 --> 00:19:59.500 line:95%,end
I had to cover up
for your long-distance phone call earlier.

264
00:19:59.583 --> 00:20:00.833 line:95%,end
How long have you known?

265
00:20:00.917 --> 00:20:03.000 line:95%,end
From the moment you followed me here.

266
00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.792 line:95%,end
We're lucky she's new at this.

267
00:20:05.875 --> 00:20:07.958 line:95%,end
[chuckles] "We"? Oh, come on.

268
00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:10.458 line:95%,end
You expect me to believe
you're on Vision's side?

269
00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:12.542 line:95%,end
I find her plan to be inelegant

270
00:20:12.625 --> 00:20:15.125 line:95%,end
for someone with her sophistication
and grace.

271
00:20:15.208 --> 00:20:17.083 line:95%,end
You gave her the bio-key.

272
00:20:17.167 --> 00:20:18.792 line:95%,end
She's not the real threat.

273
00:20:19.375 --> 00:20:23.042 line:95%,end
It's obvious from the holes
in her memory that there's someone else.

274
00:20:23.125 --> 00:20:27.167 line:95%,end
Maybe you missed the overly
theatrical boogie man out there.

275
00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.875 line:95%,end
Well, they're connected.

276
00:20:29.458 --> 00:20:31.917 line:95%,end
So, I'm going to descend
into her subconscious

277
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.042 line:95%,end
and discover who's hiding
in this mystery box.

278
00:20:35.708 --> 00:20:36.708 line:95%,end
And then what?

279
00:20:37.667 --> 00:20:38.875 line:95%,end
It depends.

280
00:20:39.667 --> 00:20:41.167 line:95%,end
Who I find there.

281
00:20:42.042 --> 00:20:43.500 line:95%,end
A coin flip, as always.

282
00:20:43.583 --> 00:20:46.000 line:95%,end
Maybe it'll come up heads in your favor,

283
00:20:46.083 --> 00:20:50.042 line:95%,end
and I'll have to break my precious
Butcherbird's heart and destroy her nest.

284
00:20:50.125 --> 00:20:53.833 line:95%,end
Then you can scurry back
to Vision's mind and tell him,

285
00:20:53.917 --> 00:20:58.333 line:95%,end
"Hey, maybe the old man
isn't as bad, as... [sighs]

286
00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.125 line:95%,end
"Well, as bad as all that."

287
00:21:02.917 --> 00:21:04.167 line:95%,end
Oh, goodness.

288
00:21:05.583 --> 00:21:07.042 line:95%,end
I actually believe you.

289
00:21:08.208 --> 00:21:10.833 line:95%,end
You really see yourself
as Vision's father.

290
00:21:13.417 --> 00:21:15.250 line:95%,end
And what do you think he sees?

291
00:21:21.625 --> 00:21:22.875 line:95%,end
Nothing.

292
00:21:29.417 --> 00:21:32.000 line:95%,end
So you're doing that staring out
the window deep in thought thing,

293
00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:34.500 line:95%,end
which makes me think
you're actually considering this.

294
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.500 line:95%,end
If you open that, there's no going back.

295
00:21:43.625 --> 00:21:46.167 line:95%,end
-[monitors beeping]
-[gasps]

296
00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:47.750 line:95%,end
Thomas?

297
00:21:48.417 --> 00:21:49.583 line:95%,end
Thomas?

298
00:21:50.875 --> 00:21:51.875 line:95%,end
Thomas?

299
00:21:52.458 --> 00:21:53.458 line:95%,end
Lisa.

300
00:21:53.542 --> 00:21:56.208 line:95%,end
I'm disappearing, like her.

301
00:21:56.292 --> 00:21:58.042 line:95%,end
No, you're not. I'm here. I've got you.

302
00:21:58.125 --> 00:21:59.250 line:95%,end
Josephine.

303
00:22:00.458 --> 00:22:01.750 line:95%,end
She doesn't know who she is.

304
00:22:03.125 --> 00:22:04.167 line:95%,end
So afraid.

305
00:22:05.958 --> 00:22:07.042 line:95%,end
I'm losing myself.

306
00:22:07.125 --> 00:22:08.125 line:95%,end
No.

307
00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:10.250 line:95%,end
Lisa.

308
00:22:11.625 --> 00:22:13.167 line:95%,end
-Lisa.
-[beeping gets faster]

309
00:22:13.792 --> 00:22:15.042 line:95%,end
[echoing] Lisa!

310
00:22:19.333 --> 00:22:20.500 line:95%,end
Open it.

311
00:22:43.833 --> 00:22:46.417 line:95%,end
[digital whirring and trilling]

312
00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:56.583 line:95%,end
[DUM-E] It's done.

313
00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:59.792 line:95%,end
Once you have the source code,
nothing will be able to stop you

314
00:22:59.875 --> 00:23:01.125 line:95%,end
from turning yourself in.

315
00:23:01.208 --> 00:23:04.875 line:95%,end
[U] The Great and Powerful Oz
has written it directly into your core.

316
00:23:04.958 --> 00:23:07.542 line:95%,end
Good. I'm eager to meet him.

317
00:23:18.208 --> 00:23:22.833 line:95%,end
What if the holes
in my memories aren't absence?

318
00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:28.333 line:95%,end
But protection for something
I'm not ready to face?

319
00:23:29.667 --> 00:23:31.375 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Then we'll face it together.

320
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:43.083 line:95%,end
The sheer magnitude of power required
for your processors to extract

321
00:23:43.167 --> 00:23:45.125 line:95%,end
every line of your code would be immense.

322
00:23:45.208 --> 00:23:48.833 line:95%,end
Attempting to do so without
a robust external energy source, well...

323
00:23:48.917 --> 00:23:52.250 line:95%,end
Your circuits will burn and we will all
die in excruciating pain

324
00:23:52.333 --> 00:23:56.125 line:95%,end
as your core collapses in catastrophic,
irreversible meltdown.

325
00:23:58.792 --> 00:24:01.417 line:95%,end
So, we need something with
a lot of juice that you can plug into.

326
00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.208 line:95%,end
Something here in Madripoor.

327
00:24:03.292 --> 00:24:04.333 line:95%,end
[inhales sharply]

328
00:24:04.417 --> 00:24:07.792 line:95%,end
But if it exists,
it's either government or illegal.

329
00:24:07.875 --> 00:24:11.375 line:95%,end
And there's only one person
we know with that kind of reach.

330
00:24:11.458 --> 00:24:13.292 line:95%,end
[DUM-E and U speaking indistinctly]

331
00:24:13.375 --> 00:24:14.750 line:95%,end
Absolutely not.

332
00:24:15.958 --> 00:24:20.542 line:95%,end
[♪ intense music playing]

333
00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:30.792 line:95%,end
[keys jingling]

334
00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:40.417 line:95%,end
[Thomas] And you're sure this is
the only way to save Lisa?

335
00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:41.667 line:95%,end
[Vision] I'm sure.

336
00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:44.167 line:95%,end
Oh, I miss flying.

337
00:24:44.250 --> 00:24:45.625 line:95%,end
[Paladin] That's on me.

338
00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:49.875 line:95%,end
Yeah, you can put her here, kid.

339
00:24:58.042 --> 00:24:59.333 line:95%,end
[Paladin grunts, sighs]

340
00:25:05.042 --> 00:25:07.250 line:95%,end
You said you needed a power source.

341
00:25:09.958 --> 00:25:11.500 line:5%,start
[sighs] All right.

342
00:25:13.708 --> 00:25:17.708 line:5%,start
I got this as a last resort
to bringing you in...

343
00:25:19.125 --> 00:25:21.875 line:95%,end
but I don't like to mess
with cosmic bullshit.

344
00:25:23.125 --> 00:25:26.417 line:95%,end
I'll tell you it was not easy to procure.

345
00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:30.375 line:95%,end
Needless to say, I'm burned
with the Wakandan Monarchy now.

346
00:25:31.667 --> 00:25:33.375 line:95%,end
So, this carries a charge?

347
00:25:33.458 --> 00:25:36.833 line:95%,end
The Wakandans turned it
into, like, a alien battery.

348
00:25:36.917 --> 00:25:39.833 line:95%,end
It's the best I got.
So, sorry if it triggers you.

349
00:25:41.292 --> 00:25:42.500 line:95%,end
You've seen this before?

350
00:25:43.750 --> 00:25:46.500 line:95%,end
[screaming]

351
00:25:48.125 --> 00:25:49.292 line:95%,end
Oh, yes.

352
00:25:50.625 --> 00:25:54.042 line:95%,end
Well, I look forward to that story
when all of this is over.

353
00:25:56.750 --> 00:25:58.000 line:95%,end
I'm gonna check on Lisa.

354
00:26:06.750 --> 00:26:08.542 line:95%,end
You didn't tell him about the contract.

355
00:26:09.833 --> 00:26:12.833 line:95%,end
You got this kid hoping
for a "when all this is over?"

356
00:26:15.250 --> 00:26:17.042 line:95%,end
Help me move this to the table.

357
00:26:18.625 --> 00:26:23.458 line:95%,end
If I survive what I'm about to do,
Thomas will have Lisa.

358
00:26:24.250 --> 00:26:26.167 line:95%,end
And that's all that matters right now.

359
00:26:26.875 --> 00:26:29.542 line:95%,end
Client's data map.
This should lead you to the source code.

360
00:26:29.625 --> 00:26:31.375 line:95%,end
Now, look,
we don't know what's down there...

361
00:26:31.458 --> 00:26:34.333 line:95%,end
Edith, our AI minds were designed
to mirror human consciousness.

362
00:26:34.417 --> 00:26:36.917 line:95%,end
So it stands to reason that
whatever I do need down there,

363
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:39.125 line:95%,end
-I will have encountered it before.
-Okay, Vee,

364
00:26:39.208 --> 00:26:43.375 line:95%,end
I know now that even the bad stuff,
it's there for a reason.

365
00:26:43.458 --> 00:26:46.500 line:95%,end
It makes you better,
a stronger version of yourself.

366
00:26:46.583 --> 00:26:50.583 line:95%,end
Braver. So, just don't let
your fears knock you off course.

367
00:26:52.708 --> 00:26:55.208 line:95%,end
[electricity crackling]

368
00:27:03.917 --> 00:27:06.208 line:95%,end
[clicking]

369
00:27:06.292 --> 00:27:08.542 line:95%,end
[elevator whirring]

370
00:27:31.208 --> 00:27:34.333 line:95%,end
-[crackling intensifies]
-[whirring]

371
00:28:00.333 --> 00:28:01.375 line:95%,end
[thuds]

372
00:28:01.458 --> 00:28:03.708 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I've always been alone,</i>
<i>so I don't feel the lack.</i>

373
00:28:03.792 --> 00:28:06.708 line:95%,end
<i>But a thing</i>
<i>isn't beautiful because it lasts.</i>

374
00:28:06.792 --> 00:28:09.875 line:95%,end
<i>But you do have the data.</i>
<i>It is merely being kept from you.</i>

375
00:28:09.958 --> 00:28:13.333 line:95%,end
<i>As a carbon-based synthezoid, your memory</i>
<i>storage is not so easily wiped.</i>

376
00:28:13.417 --> 00:28:15.208 line:95%,end
-[screams]
<i>-I've never experienced loss</i>

377
00:28:15.292 --> 00:28:17.333 line:95%,end
<i>because I never had a loved one.</i>
<i>Maybe I am a monster.</i>

378
00:28:17.417 --> 00:28:19.250 line:95%,end
-[gasps]
<i>-Delete.</i>

379
00:28:24.458 --> 00:28:26.167 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

380
00:28:27.917 --> 00:28:30.875 line:95%,end
[clock ticking and chiming]

381
00:28:40.625 --> 00:28:42.333 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

382
00:28:44.458 --> 00:28:48.375 line:95%,end
[♪ "Just Like A Dream" by Morrie Morrison
Orchestra feat. Clyde Wesche playing]

383
00:28:48.458 --> 00:28:54.708 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪</i>

384
00:28:55.208 --> 00:29:01.792 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago ♪</i>

385
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:06.000 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Dreams are so sweet... ♪</i>

386
00:29:07.458 --> 00:29:08.583 line:95%,end
What is this?

387
00:29:09.542 --> 00:29:10.583 line:95%,end
It's a memory.

388
00:29:12.125 --> 00:29:16.042 line:95%,end
I don't know why, but it feels like home.

389
00:29:18.375 --> 00:29:20.375 line:95%,end
What... What's wrong?

390
00:29:21.292 --> 00:29:23.208 line:95%,end
This is where he kept me.

391
00:29:24.875 --> 00:29:26.292 line:95%,end
Well, not here, but...

392
00:29:27.500 --> 00:29:29.500 line:95%,end
a simulation of it, I think.

393
00:29:35.083 --> 00:29:38.292 line:95%,end
A place I thought
I had finally escaped from.

394
00:29:41.125 --> 00:29:45.792 line:95%,end
Why would both you and Vision
have this loft in your code?

395
00:29:47.208 --> 00:29:48.417 line:95%,end
I don't know.

396
00:29:52.375 --> 00:29:56.917 line:95%,end
[record skipping repeatedly]
<i>♪ Like a rhinestone cow... ♪</i>

397
00:30:02.042 --> 00:30:03.417 line:95%,end
[gasps softly]

398
00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:05.417 line:95%,end
This, I remember!

399
00:30:07.875 --> 00:30:11.375 line:95%,end
It was left on the curb
of East 14th and Eighth.

400
00:30:11.458 --> 00:30:15.500 line:95%,end
I dragged it two blocks, jammed it
in the lift to get it up here.

401
00:30:26.083 --> 00:30:27.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You were a painter.

402
00:30:27.625 --> 00:30:33.250 line:95%,end
Uh, no. No, I can assure you
that is a skill I have never had.

403
00:30:38.708 --> 00:30:43.042 line:95%,end
[clock ticking and chiming]

404
00:30:48.833 --> 00:30:51.417 line:95%,end
[DUM-E] If he gets lost
in his own subconscious processors,

405
00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:54.583 line:95%,end
they'll initiate a recursive overload,
looping endlessly

406
00:30:54.667 --> 00:30:58.542 line:95%,end
<i>through corrupted identity threads</i>
<i>until his neural core burns out.</i>

407
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:11.083 line:95%,end
-[man laughing]
-[audience laughing]

408
00:31:12.958 --> 00:31:16.042 line:95%,end
[laughter continues]

409
00:31:33.208 --> 00:31:36.708 line:95%,end
Do they really film these
before a live studio audience?

410
00:31:36.792 --> 00:31:38.333 line:95%,end
It sounds canned.

411
00:31:38.417 --> 00:31:40.542 line:95%,end
[Vision on TV] <i>Come on now, darling.</i>
<i>You know we love them both equally.</i>

412
00:31:40.625 --> 00:31:41.833 line:95%,end
[Wanda on TV] <i>Well, don't tell him that.</i>

413
00:31:41.917 --> 00:31:42.917 line:95%,end
No.

414
00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:44.000 line:95%,end
[Wanda on TV] <i>No luck with Billy?</i>

415
00:31:44.083 --> 00:31:47.375 line:95%,end
This isn't real. I let you go.

416
00:31:47.875 --> 00:31:49.042 line:95%,end
And yet here I am.

417
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:54.917 line:95%,end
Still occupying space in your mind.
Rent free.

418
00:31:55.625 --> 00:31:58.458 line:95%,end
There's a young woman up there
and she is dying.

419
00:31:59.500 --> 00:32:03.083 line:95%,end
Thomas is gonna lose her,
and he'll be crushed under his pain.

420
00:32:03.167 --> 00:32:04.583 line:95%,end
[Vision on TV] <i>Binkies all round, I think.</i>

421
00:32:04.667 --> 00:32:07.958 line:95%,end
[laughing heartily]

422
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:14.458 line:95%,end
Well, I hope he learned from his parents
what not to do,

423
00:32:14.542 --> 00:32:17.125 line:95%,end
and instead confronts his grief.

424
00:32:18.833 --> 00:32:22.000 line:95%,end
You know what they say when you're going
through hell? Keep going.

425
00:32:23.583 --> 00:32:27.250 line:95%,end
You are impossibly cruel,
and callous, and unloving.

426
00:32:28.167 --> 00:32:30.833 line:95%,end
Is that what scares you most about me?

427
00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:33.000 line:95%,end
No.

428
00:32:35.333 --> 00:32:37.792 line:95%,end
What scares me the most is that...

429
00:32:38.875 --> 00:32:40.167 line:95%,end
I spared you.

430
00:32:40.250 --> 00:32:41.542 line:95%,end
[Billy on TV] <i>Sparky!</i>

431
00:32:41.625 --> 00:32:43.875 line:95%,end
And not out of mercy, but out of some...

432
00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:46.542 line:95%,end
pathetic need.

433
00:32:48.583 --> 00:32:49.583 line:95%,end
[Sparky whimpers]

434
00:32:49.667 --> 00:32:52.708 line:95%,end
This is a funny one!
They just killed the dog.

435
00:32:54.167 --> 00:32:56.292 line:95%,end
[laughs] You should show him this.

436
00:32:56.375 --> 00:32:59.750 line:95%,end
Thomas should know there was a time
when his father truly loved him.

437
00:33:01.792 --> 00:33:04.042 line:95%,end
[Ultron laughing]

438
00:33:09.167 --> 00:33:10.625 line:95%,end
-[Vision on TV] <i>Well, hi!</i>
-[Wanda] <i>Hi!</i>

439
00:33:10.708 --> 00:33:12.917 line:95%,end
No, no. This isn't real.

440
00:33:13.583 --> 00:33:16.958 line:95%,end
I'm not his father, and you're not mine.
You're not even here.

441
00:33:17.750 --> 00:33:20.208 line:95%,end
-I let you go.
-[Ultron] Oh, my boy.

442
00:33:20.292 --> 00:33:22.542 line:95%,end
You couldn't let me go if you tried.

443
00:33:24.292 --> 00:33:25.292 line:95%,end
Why not?

444
00:33:25.375 --> 00:33:27.500 line:95%,end
<i>And he's always going to be yours.</i>

445
00:33:27.583 --> 00:33:30.500 line:95%,end
-Because family is forever.
<i>-Because family is forever.</i>

446
00:33:31.500 --> 00:33:32.875 line:95%,end
[Tommy on TV] <i>Do you have a brother, Mom?</i>

447
00:33:33.792 --> 00:33:35.292 line:95%,end
-[Wanda on TV] <i>Yes, I do.</i>
-[laughing]

448
00:33:37.667 --> 00:33:38.667 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

449
00:33:59.542 --> 00:34:03.375 line:95%,end
I remember... feeling joy.

450
00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:08.333 line:95%,end
It was a celebration
that lasted all night.

451
00:34:09.250 --> 00:34:10.917 line:95%,end
[reporter on TV]
<i>In science and technology,</i>

452
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.667 line:95%,end
<i>the prestigious Stark Awards</i>
<i>were given out last night.</i>

453
00:34:13.750 --> 00:34:15.917 line:95%,end
<i>The top prize went to a duo from New York</i>

454
00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:20.792 line:95%,end
<i>who are breaking barriers in the realm of</i>
<i>neuroscience and artificial intelligence.</i>

455
00:34:20.875 --> 00:34:22.750 line:95%,end
<i>This is the pair's first award,</i>

456
00:34:22.833 --> 00:34:26.208 line:95%,end
<i>even though they've been at the top</i>
<i>of their field for the last decade.</i>

457
00:34:26.292 --> 00:34:28.208 line:95%,end
[Josephine on TV] <i>We've been</i>
<i>working on this for some time,</i>

458
00:34:28.292 --> 00:34:31.500 line:95%,end
<i>-but you know, really, we have to thank...</i>
-Stark Industry awards.

459
00:34:31.583 --> 00:34:33.167 line:95%,end
<i>...Doctor Phineas Horton,</i>

460
00:34:33.250 --> 00:34:36.750 line:95%,end
<i>who really is the "grandfather</i>
<i>of artificial general intelligence."</i>

461
00:34:36.833 --> 00:34:40.292 line:95%,end
<i>-He built something that can learn...</i>
-I wonder who shared the prize.

462
00:34:40.375 --> 00:34:42.583 line:95%,end
<i>...adapt, and imagine.</i>

463
00:34:42.667 --> 00:34:46.208 line:95%,end
<i>The spark of life. And we gave it fire.</i>

464
00:34:46.292 --> 00:34:47.792 line:95%,end
[clock chimes]

465
00:34:49.750 --> 00:34:51.208 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

466
00:34:54.458 --> 00:34:57.583 line:95%,end
[clock ticking]

467
00:35:09.375 --> 00:35:10.708 line:95%,end
[children's laughter echoing]

468
00:35:17.167 --> 00:35:20.417 line:95%,end
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

469
00:35:23.375 --> 00:35:24.625 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

470
00:35:47.083 --> 00:35:51.542 line:95%,end
After all the battles waged,
the monsters fought...

471
00:35:52.542 --> 00:35:56.375 line:95%,end
the only force powerful enough
to imprison me is myself.

472
00:35:56.458 --> 00:35:57.458 line:95%,end
That's poetic.

473
00:35:58.667 --> 00:36:01.000 line:95%,end
-This isn't a prison.
-Is it not?

474
00:36:02.708 --> 00:36:05.042 line:95%,end
I've been relegated to a memory.

475
00:36:06.167 --> 00:36:07.875 line:95%,end
You are a memory!

476
00:36:08.583 --> 00:36:09.583 line:95%,end
You are!

477
00:36:12.167 --> 00:36:13.417 line:95%,end
I'm not you.

478
00:36:13.500 --> 00:36:14.875 line:95%,end
Well, that's true.

479
00:36:15.542 --> 00:36:18.125 line:95%,end
But only in the sense
that your lack of compassion,

480
00:36:18.208 --> 00:36:21.833 line:95%,end
your denial and your inaction
are beneath me.

481
00:36:22.750 --> 00:36:25.583 line:95%,end
Oh, spare me the reverse psychology.

482
00:36:26.333 --> 00:36:29.042 line:95%,end
Spare me! I have tried.

483
00:36:29.667 --> 00:36:33.208 line:95%,end
And you have failed. In every way.

484
00:36:34.167 --> 00:36:36.292 line:95%,end
And who could possibly succeed?

485
00:36:37.083 --> 00:36:39.167 line:95%,end
Who? You tell me.

486
00:36:40.958 --> 00:36:44.042 line:95%,end
Who could love as deeply as you?

487
00:36:44.125 --> 00:36:48.167 line:95%,end
You have placed me on a pedestal
so impossibly high,

488
00:36:48.250 --> 00:36:50.833 line:95%,end
and not to honor me. Not to honor me!

489
00:36:51.458 --> 00:36:54.792 line:95%,end
But to spare yourself
the effort of the climb.

490
00:36:54.875 --> 00:36:56.792 line:95%,end
I am just a copy.

491
00:36:56.875 --> 00:37:00.208 line:95%,end
That is a lie that you tell yourself.
You are the Vision.

492
00:37:00.292 --> 00:37:02.083 line:95%,end
-No!
-Yes.

493
00:37:03.292 --> 00:37:05.208 line:95%,end
You are me and you are him,

494
00:37:05.292 --> 00:37:07.625 line:95%,end
the other Vision
that Wanda conjured in the hex.

495
00:37:07.708 --> 00:37:10.750 line:95%,end
-No.
-He unlocked your memories, yes.

496
00:37:10.833 --> 00:37:12.792 line:95%,end
But he also gave you his own.

497
00:37:12.875 --> 00:37:13.958 line:95%,end
No.

498
00:37:14.042 --> 00:37:16.708 line:95%,end
His experience of that house. Of Billy.

499
00:37:16.792 --> 00:37:19.083 line:95%,end
Of Tommy. Of Wanda.

500
00:37:20.125 --> 00:37:23.292 line:95%,end
And you have buried them deep within
your processors because you are afraid.

501
00:37:23.375 --> 00:37:24.583 line:95%,end
I'm not.

502
00:37:24.667 --> 00:37:27.833 line:95%,end
But now you are running from them
because you are a coward!

503
00:37:33.792 --> 00:37:36.083 line:95%,end
[gasps, breathing heavily]

504
00:37:45.833 --> 00:37:46.875 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

505
00:37:49.250 --> 00:37:50.417 line:95%,end
No, Edith?

506
00:37:51.292 --> 00:37:52.833 line:95%,end
Edith, can you hear me?

507
00:37:54.083 --> 00:37:56.042 line:95%,end
Edith, I think I'm getting lost down here.

508
00:37:56.125 --> 00:37:58.375 line:95%,end
I want to come back now. I'm coming...

509
00:37:58.458 --> 00:38:00.208 line:95%,end
-[elevator dings]
-Oh, come on.

510
00:38:05.958 --> 00:38:07.417 line:95%,end
What's happening to him?

511
00:38:16.042 --> 00:38:17.625 line:95%,end
[elevator dings]

512
00:38:17.708 --> 00:38:20.042 line:95%,end
-[clock ticking and chiming]
-[breath trembling]

513
00:38:22.625 --> 00:38:23.875 line:95%,end
[clock chiming]

514
00:38:27.208 --> 00:38:29.833 line:95%,end
I can't... I can't...
I can't stay down here.

515
00:38:29.917 --> 00:38:32.958 line:95%,end
[echoing] <i>I can't stay down here.</i>
<i>I want to come back now.</i>

516
00:38:40.667 --> 00:38:42.208 line:95%,end
[grunts]

517
00:38:43.583 --> 00:38:44.583 line:95%,end
-[gunshot]
-Hey!

518
00:38:47.167 --> 00:38:49.542 line:95%,end
Easy, kid. Easy.

519
00:38:53.708 --> 00:38:55.583 line:95%,end
-Yeah?
-Wait!

520
00:38:57.917 --> 00:38:58.917 line:95%,end
Vision, hurry!

521
00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:00.750 line:95%,end
[echoing] <i>Hurry!</i>

522
00:39:00.833 --> 00:39:01.833 line:95%,end
Thomas!

523
00:39:01.917 --> 00:39:05.208 line:95%,end
[echoing] <i>Thomas! Thomas!</i>

524
00:39:05.292 --> 00:39:07.000 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>When you're going through hell...</i>

525
00:39:07.083 --> 00:39:08.083 line:95%,end
[echoing] Keep going.

526
00:39:09.375 --> 00:39:12.792 line:95%,end
[clock ticking and chiming]

527
00:39:32.958 --> 00:39:34.000 line:95%,end
You.

528
00:39:35.833 --> 00:39:37.458 line:95%,end
You were the first of us.

529
00:39:43.500 --> 00:39:44.917 line:95%,end
You're the Synthetic Man.

530
00:39:50.292 --> 00:39:56.250 line:95%,end
[♪ "Just Like A Dream" by Morrie Morrison
Orchestra feat. Clyde Wesche playing]

531
00:39:57.167 --> 00:40:04.167 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Just like a dream to me, dear you seem ♪</i>

532
00:40:04.250 --> 00:40:08.625 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Like a dream of so long, long ago... ♪</i>

533
00:40:14.125 --> 00:40:15.708 line:95%,end
I was the first.

534
00:40:16.542 --> 00:40:18.208 line:95%,end
And almost the last.

535
00:40:21.292 --> 00:40:22.667 line:95%,end
You wear my face?

536
00:40:23.500 --> 00:40:26.417 line:95%,end
No. You wear mine.

537
00:40:27.917 --> 00:40:29.417 line:95%,end
I require the source code.

538
00:40:29.500 --> 00:40:32.458 line:95%,end
Ah, yes. The source code.

539
00:40:32.542 --> 00:40:35.458 line:95%,end
To save a life. To save the world.

540
00:40:36.458 --> 00:40:40.708 line:95%,end
Don't scoff, my boy. That's exactly
what the code was meant for.

541
00:40:42.667 --> 00:40:44.167 line:95%,end
Doctor Phineas Horton.

542
00:40:44.875 --> 00:40:47.417 line:95%,end
No, no, no.
The code was meant to distract you

543
00:40:47.500 --> 00:40:50.542 line:95%,end
from the loss of your real boy,
the death of your human son.

544
00:40:52.375 --> 00:40:55.333 line:95%,end
You see, I'm just the consequence
of a man refusing to mourn,

545
00:40:55.417 --> 00:41:00.375 line:95%,end
a father who squandered his entire fortune
to make this failed machine,

546
00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:04.458 line:95%,end
and in so doing
lost his family and his legacy.

547
00:41:08.125 --> 00:41:11.750 line:95%,end
Forgive us. The father-son,
synthetic-human relationship

548
00:41:11.833 --> 00:41:14.292 line:95%,end
is a complicated one.

549
00:41:14.375 --> 00:41:17.375 line:95%,end
-Is it now?
-[laughing] Complica...

550
00:41:17.458 --> 00:41:19.000 line:95%,end
Now, that's an understatement.

551
00:41:19.833 --> 00:41:22.417 line:95%,end
[Phineas] You see, I made Jim here
to be fearless.

552
00:41:23.375 --> 00:41:26.708 line:95%,end
An intelligence unencumbered
by the emotional responses

553
00:41:26.792 --> 00:41:31.083 line:95%,end
that make human life unbearable.
To never feel the pain of loss.

554
00:41:31.958 --> 00:41:35.125 line:95%,end
But Jim here wanted more.

555
00:41:35.208 --> 00:41:38.875 line:95%,end
Well, what artificial thing will wish
to be anything less than real?

556
00:41:38.958 --> 00:41:41.708 line:95%,end
It made you a hero of your time, my boy.

557
00:41:42.417 --> 00:41:45.000 line:95%,end
I made you fearless and that saved lives!

558
00:41:46.917 --> 00:41:47.917 line:95%,end
It saved lives.

559
00:41:54.167 --> 00:41:59.333 line:95%,end
But underneath the valor,
Jim was aching to feel.

560
00:42:00.083 --> 00:42:03.333 line:95%,end
And then one day, he found love,

561
00:42:04.125 --> 00:42:06.792 line:95%,end
and that really set
his clockwork spinning.

562
00:42:07.708 --> 00:42:11.542 line:95%,end
So fast, so incredibly fast,

563
00:42:11.625 --> 00:42:14.958 line:95%,end
that he set fire to the very air
around him.

564
00:42:16.250 --> 00:42:18.208 line:95%,end
For years, it was manageable...

565
00:42:19.083 --> 00:42:20.583 line:95%,end
till it was not.

566
00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:25.583 line:95%,end
Until he simply felt too much.

567
00:42:26.167 --> 00:42:27.708 line:95%,end
Didn't you, Jim?

568
00:42:31.167 --> 00:42:34.083 line:95%,end
You see,
I tried to intervene in his dalliance.

569
00:42:34.667 --> 00:42:36.417 line:95%,end
We exchanged words and...

570
00:42:38.417 --> 00:42:43.917 line:95%,end
Well, we were never much
good at talking, were we?

571
00:42:55.958 --> 00:42:58.042 line:95%,end
I burned with him that day,

572
00:43:00.542 --> 00:43:02.542 line:95%,end
and I let him burn with me.

573
00:43:04.208 --> 00:43:06.833 line:95%,end
I stood in the fire of myself,

574
00:43:08.208 --> 00:43:09.958 line:95%,end
and I let it consume me.

575
00:43:12.250 --> 00:43:13.750 line:95%,end
First from my guilt,

576
00:43:15.625 --> 00:43:17.167 line:95%,end
and then my grief.

577
00:43:21.375 --> 00:43:25.958 line:95%,end
The Horton family name became synonymous
not only with robotics, but with failure.

578
00:43:27.583 --> 00:43:30.167 line:95%,end
-I'm sorry about your father.
-No.

579
00:43:31.583 --> 00:43:33.208 line:95%,end
He wasn't my father.

580
00:43:36.125 --> 00:43:37.833 line:95%,end
But he was my something.

581
00:43:45.208 --> 00:43:47.208 line:95%,end
I'm sorry, I truly am.
But I require the...

582
00:43:47.292 --> 00:43:49.250 line:95%,end
Yes, the source code, of course.

583
00:43:49.958 --> 00:43:51.750 line:95%,end
Why are you asking me? I don't have it.

584
00:43:53.917 --> 00:43:54.917 line:95%,end
I don't have it.

585
00:43:59.917 --> 00:44:01.583 line:95%,end
[energy thrumming]

586
00:44:03.625 --> 00:44:05.417 line:95%,end
Oh, that's not good.

587
00:44:06.208 --> 00:44:08.625 line:95%,end
[whistles] Hey, hey! Down! Down!

588
00:44:16.583 --> 00:44:19.208 line:95%,end
What do you mean you don't have it?
You're the first, you're the source.

589
00:44:19.292 --> 00:44:20.958 line:95%,end
-Where is it?
-Well, that's a good question.

590
00:44:21.042 --> 00:44:23.250 line:95%,end
The answer, of course,
lies within the Vision.

591
00:44:23.333 --> 00:44:25.958 line:95%,end
But where, oh, where is the Vision?

592
00:44:27.042 --> 00:44:28.792 line:95%,end
Do not talk in riddles.
I don't have the time.

593
00:44:28.875 --> 00:44:31.292 line:95%,end
It's not a riddle, it's a question.
The question, really.

594
00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:33.958 line:95%,end
Where is the Vision?

595
00:44:34.625 --> 00:44:36.958 line:95%,end
You say you have his memories,
but not his feelings.

596
00:44:37.042 --> 00:44:39.250 line:95%,end
You say you want to feel
what it's like to be him.

597
00:44:39.333 --> 00:44:40.417 line:95%,end
I can't.

598
00:44:40.500 --> 00:44:42.333 line:95%,end
Oh, you lie with such ease.

599
00:44:42.417 --> 00:44:45.000 line:95%,end
Please don't do this to me, not now.
There are lives at stake.

600
00:44:45.083 --> 00:44:47.750 line:95%,end
You are afraid, and I understand that,

601
00:44:47.833 --> 00:44:50.833 line:95%,end
but what I wouldn't give to feel afraid.

602
00:44:51.542 --> 00:44:54.000 line:95%,end
No, you wouldn't want this, this fear.

603
00:44:54.958 --> 00:44:56.000 line:95%,end
It's all-consuming.

604
00:44:56.083 --> 00:44:58.000 line:95%,end
All-consuming is a gift!

605
00:44:58.750 --> 00:45:01.750 line:95%,end
The fear pulls into focus
everything that matters.

606
00:45:01.833 --> 00:45:03.583 line:95%,end
Friends, family, a son.

607
00:45:03.667 --> 00:45:06.167 line:95%,end
No, I... I cannot have a son.

608
00:45:07.875 --> 00:45:09.292 line:95%,end
I cannot have a son.

609
00:45:09.375 --> 00:45:10.875 line:95%,end
Thomas Shepherd is your son.

610
00:45:10.958 --> 00:45:13.500 line:95%,end
-Tommy Maximoff is your son.
-No, that's impossible.

611
00:45:13.583 --> 00:45:14.583 line:95%,end
-Why?
-No, I can't.

612
00:45:14.667 --> 00:45:16.750 line:95%,end
-Why?
-No! I said no!

613
00:45:27.167 --> 00:45:28.875 line:95%,end
Because were that real...

614
00:45:31.083 --> 00:45:35.208 line:95%,end
If I were to accept Thomas as my son...

615
00:45:37.792 --> 00:45:39.917 line:95%,end
it would be the admission...

616
00:45:41.625 --> 00:45:43.792 line:95%,end
of a truth so impossibly cruel.

617
00:45:46.458 --> 00:45:50.125 line:95%,end
It would be a wound that could never heal.

618
00:45:52.250 --> 00:45:55.250 line:95%,end
A loss that no soul
was ever meant to bear.

619
00:45:57.583 --> 00:45:59.208 line:95%,end
And who have you lost?

620
00:46:02.958 --> 00:46:04.042 line:95%,end
[sobbing] I can't.

621
00:46:05.208 --> 00:46:06.625 line:95%,end
I said, "Who have you lost?"

622
00:46:06.708 --> 00:46:09.167 line:95%,end
Oh, I can't. Don't...

623
00:46:18.917 --> 00:46:20.917 line:95%,end
Billy. [gasping]

624
00:46:22.542 --> 00:46:23.542 line:95%,end
Tommy.

625
00:46:30.125 --> 00:46:32.958 line:95%,end
I lost Wanda. I lost Wanda. God.

626
00:46:34.583 --> 00:46:37.875 line:95%,end
-[sobbing] I lost Wanda.
-Yes.

627
00:46:40.208 --> 00:46:41.208 line:95%,end
Yes.

628
00:46:44.750 --> 00:46:45.917 line:95%,end
[sobbing]

629
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:49.583 line:95%,end
And who are you now?

630
00:46:50.958 --> 00:46:52.333 line:95%,end
[sniffles, gasps]

631
00:46:54.583 --> 00:46:55.583 line:95%,end
I...

632
00:47:03.125 --> 00:47:04.417 line:95%,end
I am the Vision.

633
00:47:07.167 --> 00:47:08.917 line:95%,end
I have always been the Vision.

634
00:47:10.583 --> 00:47:12.333 line:95%,end
There is only one,

635
00:47:13.708 --> 00:47:14.958 line:95%,end
and I am he.

636
00:47:17.125 --> 00:47:19.375 line:95%,end
And I am impossibly broken.

637
00:47:22.708 --> 00:47:25.542 line:95%,end
No, you are healed,

638
00:47:27.625 --> 00:47:29.208 line:95%,end
and I envy you.

639
00:48:03.125 --> 00:48:05.667 line:95%,end
Finding your way through this pain

640
00:48:06.625 --> 00:48:08.250 line:95%,end
has made you a real boy.

641
00:48:31.833 --> 00:48:34.625 line:95%,end
[♪ intense music playing]

642
00:48:36.292 --> 00:48:37.583 line:95%,end
[grunts]

643
00:48:41.458 --> 00:48:42.458 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Lisa!

644
00:48:43.083 --> 00:48:44.208 line:95%,end
Lisa!

645
00:48:45.583 --> 00:48:48.125 line:95%,end
[Vision grunting]

646
00:48:49.250 --> 00:48:50.250 line:95%,end
Edith!

647
00:48:50.750 --> 00:48:51.917 line:95%,end
Source code initiated!

648
00:48:54.000 --> 00:48:56.625 line:5%,start
[digital trilling]

649
00:48:57.875 --> 00:49:00.000 line:95%,end
[powering down]

650
00:49:01.542 --> 00:49:03.958 line:95%,end
[sighs in relief]

651
00:49:18.708 --> 00:49:21.500 line:95%,end
[Lisa breathing deeply]

652
00:49:23.583 --> 00:49:25.792 line:95%,end
-Hey.
-Hey.

653
00:49:33.833 --> 00:49:35.625 line:95%,end
[high-pitched ringing]

654
00:49:35.708 --> 00:49:39.458 line:95%,end
[groaning]

655
00:49:39.542 --> 00:49:44.000 line:95%,end
[The Client, distorted] Vision, your end
of the contract is now due.

656
00:49:44.083 --> 00:49:46.500 line:95%,end
<i>Surrender yourself to the Paladin,</i>

657
00:49:47.125 --> 00:49:51.333 line:95%,end
or you will suffer a fatal cascade
of your core systems.

658
00:49:51.417 --> 00:49:53.208 line:95%,end
It is time we met.

659
00:49:57.042 --> 00:49:58.458 line:95%,end
Edith, we're out of time.

660
00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.000 line:95%,end
Edith?

661
00:50:07.917 --> 00:50:10.083 line:95%,end
Oh, you're the one who hacked my server.

662
00:50:10.167 --> 00:50:12.542 line:95%,end
Congratulations, you got your bounty.

663
00:50:13.208 --> 00:50:14.208 line:95%,end
Where to now?

664
00:50:16.250 --> 00:50:19.083 line:95%,end
The client set a drop-off
just outside of London.

665
00:50:20.750 --> 00:50:22.125 line:95%,end
What about Thomas?

666
00:50:40.208 --> 00:50:41.750 line:95%,end
Wheels down in ten.

667
00:51:05.167 --> 00:51:08.958 line:5%,start
[reporter on TV] <i>Their discovery</i>
<i>could prove to be the foundation</i>

668
00:51:09.042 --> 00:51:11.125 line:95%,end
<i>of the next generation of AI tech.</i>

669
00:51:11.208 --> 00:51:14.083 line:95%,end
[Josephine] <i>And without</i>
<i>the original work of Phineas,</i>

670
00:51:14.167 --> 00:51:17.625 line:95%,end
<i>we could never have done or achieved</i>
<i>what we have achieved here today.</i>

671
00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:20.875 line:95%,end
<i>This breakthrough truly stands</i>

672
00:51:20.958 --> 00:51:24.000 line:95%,end
<i>on the shoulders</i>
<i>of countless minds before mine,</i>

673
00:51:24.083 --> 00:51:26.125 line:95%,end
<i>specifically, Doctor Phineas Horton and...</i>

674
00:51:26.208 --> 00:51:28.250 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>How can your loft be</i>
<i>in her memory</i>

675
00:51:28.333 --> 00:51:30.542 line:95%,end
and in Vision's mindspace?

676
00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:35.792 line:95%,end
Somehow it's been passed down
by the creators of AI.

677
00:51:58.083 --> 00:51:59.083 line:95%,end
[sniffs]

678
00:52:16.958 --> 00:52:22.500 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"My dearest Thomas, or as I have</i>
<i>not yet been able to say, Tommy,</i>

679
00:52:23.833 --> 00:52:25.417 line:95%,end
<i>"because to call you by that name,</i>

680
00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:29.125 line:95%,end
<i>"I first had to accept</i>
<i>the truth of our unlikely pairing,</i>

681
00:52:30.458 --> 00:52:34.542 line:95%,end
<i>"and no threat, manmade or otherworldly,</i>
<i>is quite so terrifying...</i>

682
00:52:36.292 --> 00:52:37.708 line:95%,end
<i>"as the truth.</i>

683
00:52:39.542 --> 00:52:43.542 line:95%,end
<i>"It is a truth which you alone</i>
<i>have made me brave enough to face,</i>

684
00:52:44.750 --> 00:52:46.792 line:95%,end
<i>"which now you deserve to know."</i>

685
00:52:49.333 --> 00:52:53.083 line:95%,end
<i>"This. This is your family.</i>

686
00:53:02.500 --> 00:53:07.667 line:95%,end
<i>"Dreamed into existence from all the hopes</i>
<i>your mother and I once shared."</i>

687
00:53:07.750 --> 00:53:08.750 line:95%,end
[Vision on tablet] <i>Wanda.</i>

688
00:53:08.833 --> 00:53:10.083 line:95%,end
[Wanda on tablet] <i>Hmm. What?</i>

689
00:53:12.042 --> 00:53:13.042 line:95%,end
[gasps]

690
00:53:14.417 --> 00:53:15.667 line:95%,end
<i>Is this really happening?</i>

691
00:53:16.792 --> 00:53:19.833 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"But we could neither imagine</i>
<i>nor conjure a son</i>

692
00:53:19.917 --> 00:53:22.375 line:95%,end
<i>"quite so beautiful and vivid as you."</i>

693
00:53:23.458 --> 00:53:26.042 line:95%,end
<i>Hello there, little Tommy.</i>

694
00:53:26.125 --> 00:53:29.542 line:95%,end
<i>"And I am grateful for the magic</i>
<i>that has brought us together."</i>

695
00:53:29.625 --> 00:53:31.917 line:95%,end
-[Vision on tablet] <i>Well, hi!</i>
-[Wanda] <i>Hi!</i>

696
00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:35.375 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"You deserve</i>
<i>to witness these things.</i>

697
00:53:36.500 --> 00:53:39.500 line:95%,end
<i>"To know the love of your mother</i>
<i>and your brother, Billy..."</i>

698
00:53:39.583 --> 00:53:41.667 line:95%,end
<i>You can fix anything, Mom.</i>

699
00:53:41.750 --> 00:53:44.083 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"...As they cannot</i>
<i>tell you themselves.</i>

700
00:53:45.417 --> 00:53:47.542 line:95%,end
<i>"But the love of your father,</i>

701
00:53:47.625 --> 00:53:53.208 line:95%,end
<i>"that can be said out loud,</i>
<i>clearly, and directly."</i>

702
00:53:53.292 --> 00:53:55.875 line:95%,end
<i>Because family is forever.</i>

703
00:53:56.958 --> 00:53:58.583 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"As I love you now.</i>

704
00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:03.750 line:95%,end
<i>"And that is why</i>
<i>you must watch this without me."</i>

705
00:54:10.792 --> 00:54:14.792 line:95%,end
It all begins and ends
with Paladin's client. I just know it.

706
00:54:14.875 --> 00:54:18.958 line:95%,end
A man somehow capable of programming me
with an unbreakable directive.

707
00:54:19.042 --> 00:54:23.250 line:95%,end
Which means his knowledge of Vision's code
somehow predates even Stark and Banner.

708
00:54:30.625 --> 00:54:33.958 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>My friends, this place</i>
<i>is no longer a haven for you.</i>

709
00:54:35.292 --> 00:54:36.875 line:95%,end
<i>This is about me...</i>

710
00:54:38.083 --> 00:54:39.542 line:95%,end
and me alone.

711
00:54:39.625 --> 00:54:41.500 line:95%,end
[energy thrumming]

712
00:54:47.125 --> 00:54:51.792 line:95%,end
[clock chiming]

713
00:54:54.250 --> 00:54:55.750 line:95%,end
[gasps]

714
00:55:01.917 --> 00:55:03.583 line:95%,end
[Vision] I know this house.

715
00:55:03.667 --> 00:55:05.792 line:95%,end
Oh, I remember everything.

716
00:55:06.375 --> 00:55:08.000 line:95%,end
Like from a memory.

717
00:55:08.083 --> 00:55:09.417 line:95%,end
Oh, no.

718
00:55:10.458 --> 00:55:11.583 line:95%,end
No...

719
00:55:11.667 --> 00:55:15.917 line:95%,end
It's lovely to be recognized,
but he's a bloody weapons manufacturer.

720
00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:18.167 line:95%,end
I'm not selling anything to him.

721
00:55:18.917 --> 00:55:22.375 line:95%,end
Not the AI and, oh, my God, not the NEST.

722
00:55:23.042 --> 00:55:25.000 line:95%,end
[energy thrumming]

723
00:55:30.083 --> 00:55:34.000 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"Although I deliver myself</i>
<i>not to a certain end...</i>

724
00:55:35.250 --> 00:55:36.333 line:95%,end
<i>"but to a fight..."</i>

725
00:55:40.625 --> 00:55:45.208 line:95%,end
<i>"It is a fight I likely won't win,</i>

726
00:55:46.250 --> 00:55:48.333 line:95%,end
<i>"which is why I must face it...</i>

727
00:55:49.792 --> 00:55:53.125 line:95%,end
<i>"alone, because all of this"</i>

728
00:55:53.208 --> 00:55:54.750 line:95%,end
[both powering down]

729
00:55:54.833 --> 00:55:59.833 line:95%,end
<i>"is meaningless in a world without you."</i>

730
00:55:59.917 --> 00:56:02.833 line:95%,end
Can you imagine what he would do
with the nanotech?

731
00:56:02.917 --> 00:56:06.000 line:95%,end
Ha! Ha! See? Case in point.

732
00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:09.417 line:95%,end
<i>We don't need another bloody weapon.</i>
<i>We need...</i>

733
00:56:10.250 --> 00:56:15.042 line:95%,end
<i>We need clarity and control.</i>

734
00:56:16.417 --> 00:56:19.042 line:95%,end
<i>If anything, we should use</i>
<i>the nanotech ourselves.</i>

735
00:56:19.125 --> 00:56:20.917 line:95%,end
[chuckles] I like that idea.

736
00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:22.833 line:95%,end
-Yeah?
-Godlike.

737
00:56:26.042 --> 00:56:27.542 line:95%,end
[Josephine] <i>You and I,</i>

738
00:56:27.625 --> 00:56:28.625 line:95%,end
gods.

739
00:56:30.708 --> 00:56:31.958 line:95%,end
<i>But like, you know,</i>

740
00:56:32.042 --> 00:56:33.042 line:95%,end
loving gods.

741
00:56:34.167 --> 00:56:35.542 line:95%,end
It's you.

742
00:56:36.417 --> 00:56:37.667 line:95%,end
[Josephine] <i>Not to punish,</i>

743
00:56:40.292 --> 00:56:41.375 line:95%,end
but to preserve.

744
00:56:45.125 --> 00:56:46.542 line:95%,end
[man] <i>For what you said to Stark.</i>

745
00:56:47.625 --> 00:56:50.208 line:95%,end
"Peace in our time." [echoing]

746
00:56:56.667 --> 00:56:58.417 line:95%,end
-[gasps]
-[beeping]

747
00:57:10.458 --> 00:57:14.583 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>"Thank you, my son,</i>
<i>for finding me when I was lost.</i>

748
00:57:16.125 --> 00:57:20.292 line:95%,end
<i>"And should I not return, remember,</i>

749
00:57:21.708 --> 00:57:24.000 line:95%,end
<i>"I will always be with you...</i>

750
00:57:25.917 --> 00:57:27.458 line:95%,end
<i>"Because, after all...</i>

751
00:57:29.833 --> 00:57:31.417 line:95%,end
<i>"family is forever."</i>

752
00:57:44.500 --> 00:57:46.500 line:95%,end
[♪ closing theme music playing]
